    "Karar (duzeltme turu 2): A^sigma_scr and I^sigma are written 'A(sigma, scr)' and 'I(sigma)' (function notation, Greek sigma), because mathtext super- and subscripts print at 70 % and fall under the 8 pt floor (trap 6), and a bare 'A' would read as the A^rho of estimates_forest; the caption maps A(sigma, scr) = A^sigma_scr, I(sigma) = I^sigma.",
